Now to me , this was always going to be a typographic solution , what I would call the opposite of Type 101 .
What does that mean ?
Usually on the first day of Introduction to Typography , you get the assignment of , select a word and make it look like what it says it is . So that &apos;s Type 101 , right ?
Very simple stuff .
This is going to be the opposite of that .
I want this book to look like it &apos;s lying to you , desperately and hopelessly , the way an alcoholic would .
The answer was the most low-tech thing you can imagine .
I set up the type , I printed it out on an Epson printer with water-soluble ink , taped it to the wall and threw a bucket of water at it . Presto !
