I &apos;m starting the story with the first atomic bomb at Trinity , which was the Manhattan Project . It was a little bit like TED : it brought a whole lot of very smart people together .
And three of the smartest people were Stan Ulam , Richard Feynman and John von Neumann .
And it was Von Neumann who said , after the bomb , he was working on something much more important than bombs : he &apos;s thinking about computers .
